## Session 9 summary

**4/tcp went from 14/17 to 17/17 (achieved twice — runs r5, r7), with four root-caused, RULE-4-proven fixes on build `2493D345`:**

1. **FIX-26 (v1→v3)** — the dir_reuse one-name loss root: `bast_process` released a **mid-drain upgrade grant** (entry captured for the PR tenure; the pending EX gen=98 landed during the drain; the holders re-check passed because the woken waiter hadn't incremented yet) → phantom cached EX → **two nodes allocated the same dirent slot (aoff=184) 1.8ms apart**, last writer erased the peer's name. Fix: capture the tenure gen at bast entry and abort the release when it moved; v3 keeps the fresh grant CACHED and arms `i_dlm_bast_pending` so the last `ilock_end` re-fires the release (v2 without that collapsed tds pace to 18/150 rounds via 6s peer-retry stalls).
2. **FIX-27** — test1's kernel panic (serial-log captured: stack guard page, ~35 recursive `mxfs_dlm_ilock_begin` frames): the EDEADLK retry tail-recursed; converted to a bounded `goto` loop with backoff and a shutdown cap.
3. **FIX-25 widened** — test2's 900s wedge (live 3-task cycle: bast drain in `folio_wait_writeback` ← ioend needs EX ← demote-wait refused at PR): the ioend admit now accepts a PR-granted mirror (PR excludes peer EX) without elevating the cached mode.
4. **FIX-28** — the deferred-publish loop was claiming **~1000 phantom master-EX ghosts per node per run** (`pre_mode != EX`); the P78 probe is now a guard that skips the claim when the FS-layer EX is gone.

Also added durable diagnostics: P9-LFREE dirent-free ledger, realns on P13-LADD, P9-NLEDGE s_remove_count skew ledger; and documented that VM serial logs (`/var/log/libvirt/qemu/testN-serial.log`) capture panics but are truncated on domain start.

**Remaining for the criteria:** one residual 4/tcp flake — a **mass single-block revert** (r8 round 13: 59 names, node1's f4-f50 + peers' f9-f14, md5s intact = one data block reverted to its birth-era image; daddr-reuse ABA class). A 3× standalone dir_reuse repro loop with full ledgers is running now (`scratchpad/drc_loop_r9.log`). After 4/tcp is consistent: 8/tcp, then 2/tcp and 1/tcp. All state and next steps are in ccmemory (`sess9run-HEAD-r8-mass-block-revert-next-steps`).

